 ## Compute-unit / priority fee tuning
 
-Since the OpenBook removal an AMM v4 swap no longer validates any market state, so a V1 `SwapBaseIn` is markedly cheaper than it used to be — and `SwapBaseInV2` (8 accounts, no market placeholders) is cheaper still. Measure your own path rather than budgeting off historical figures, and always pass an explicit compute-unit limit:
+In a Triton mainnet sample collected on 2026-11-20, the program's own median consumption was 15,397 CU for 98 `SwapBaseInV2` calls and 16,091 CU for 34 v1 `SwapBaseIn` calls.
+
+Compute use still depends on the complete transaction. ATA creation, wSOL wrapping, and other instructions add to the AMM v4 swap itself. The priority fee is charged on the compute-unit limit you request, not on what the transaction uses, so an oversized limit costs money. Simulate the transaction you built, add headroom, and pass the resulting limit explicitly:
 
 ```ts
 const { execute, transaction } = await raydium.liquidity.swap({
   /* ...params... */
   computeBudgetConfig: {
-    units: 400_000,
+    units: 100_000,              // headroom over the swap plus ATA setup; size it from a simulation
     microLamports: 50_000,       // priority fee per CU
   },
 });
 ```
 
-If you omit `computeBudgetConfig`, the SDK may still use its own default; inspect the returned `transaction` to confirm. See [`integration-guides/priority-fee-tuning`](/integration-guides/priority-fee-tuning).
+For legacy and `TxVersion.V0` transactions, omitting `computeBudgetConfig` makes `0.2.85-alpha` add no Compute Budget instruction. The transaction uses Solana's runtime default limit and pays no priority fee.
+
+`TxVersion.V1` behaves differently. Its compute limit and priority fee live in the V1 transaction configuration, not in ordinary Compute Budget instructions. If you omit `computeBudgetConfig`, the V1 builder requests the SDK's default priority-fee configuration and falls back to a 600,000 CU limit. The resulting V1 transaction can therefore pay a priority fee even though it has no Compute Budget instruction. See [`integration-guides/priority-fee-tuning`](/integration-guides/priority-fee-tuning).
 
