 ## Collection
 
-The admin (Raydium multisig) calls `WithdrawPnl` to sweep `need_take_pnl_*` into the pool-level "PnL owner" accounts configured on the program's `AmmConfig` (a different, program-scoped config — not the per-pool CPMM-style AmmConfig). Sweeping:
+`WithdrawPnl` sweeps the protocol fee. The signer must be the program admin (`amm_owner`) or the `pnl_owner` stored on the program-wide `AmmConfig`. The caller supplies the two destination token accounts; the program checks only that their mints match the pool's. It works in any status except `Uninitialized`. It:
 
-1. Transfers `need_take_pnl_coin` / `need_take_pnl_pc` from the pool vaults to the PnL destination.
-2. Zeroes the counters.
+1. Realises PnL first: runs `calc_take_pnl`, which adds the protocol's share of the growth since the last baseline to `need_take_pnl_*`.
+2. Transfers the full `need_take_pnl_coin` / `need_take_pnl_pc` from the pool vaults to the destination accounts. If either exceeds its vault balance, the call fails with `TakePnlError`.
+3. Zeroes the counters and resets the `TargetOrders` baseline.
 
-There is no longer an OpenBook-settle step. If the vault balance is insufficient to cover the accrued PnL, the instruction now returns `TakePnlError` directly. The operation does not move the curve — LPs should not see any price change across a `WithdrawPnl` call. Note the `WithdrawPnl` account layout changed in the 2026-07 upgrade (see [instructions](/products/amm-v4/instructions#withdrawpnl-/-takepnl)).
+When step 1 books new PnL, it takes those tokens out of the curve's reserves, so **`k` shrinks**. The price doesn't move, because both sides shrink in proportion. Paying out PnL booked earlier doesn't change `k`, because the curve already excluded it. The `WithdrawPnl` account layout changed in the 2026-07 upgrade (see [instructions](/products/amm-v4/instructions#withdrawpnl)).
 
 ## LP fee redemption
 
-There is no dedicated "collect LP fees" instruction. LP fees accumulate in the vaults and inflate `k` over time; LPs realize them by burning LP tokens via `Withdraw`. The value of an LP token grows monotonically as `(coin_reserve_effective, pc_reserve_effective)` grow.
+There is no dedicated "collect LP fees" instruction. LP fees stay in the vaults and raise `k`; LPs collect them by burning LP tokens via `Withdraw`. Swap fees add to the reserves behind each LP token. Booking protocol PnL takes a smaller amount back out. With the default parameters, that amount is 12% of the growth. Neither value tells you an LP token's market value, which also moves with the prices of the two tokens.
 
