+---
+title: "CLMM docs updates"
+description: "Every correction to the CLMM chapter, grouped by why it was needed, with the old and new wording and links to the changed section and to the source behind it."
+---
+
+- 2026-11-22 · **[CLMM chapter](/products/clmm):** Corrects seven of the eight CLMM pages against the program source, the published SDK and mainnet. No upstream PR has been opened. The changes are in this checkout.
+
+**In short.** The CLMM pages described the program's overall structure largely accurately, but several behavior claims and some account-table details did not match the source. The fee-tier table had indexes 0–2 wrong. The math and fees pages said fees always come off the input, but nearly half the busiest pools take them from one fixed token. They said limit-order fills are fee-free and happen after the tick is crossed; both are wrong. Several pages said swaps and increase-liquidity create tick arrays, that a decrease closes a filled limit order, and that out-of-range positions can earn rewards. The code demos had one example that does not type-check against the SDK.
+
+## Pages edited
+
+- [Overview](/products/clmm/overview): corrects the opening cost, the limit-order and OpenBook statements, and when fees are paid.
+- [Accounts](/products/clmm/accounts): corrects the fee-tier table, tick-array creation, the bitmap extension, NFT ownership and the lifecycle table.
+- [Ticks and positions](/products/clmm/ticks-and-positions): corrects tick-array creation and cost, NFT authority and metadata, and out-of-range rewards.
+- [Math](/products/clmm/math): corrects the step fee, limit-order matching and settlement, the dynamic-fee decay rule and the price-limit behavior.
+- [Instructions](/products/clmm/instructions): corrects `CreatePool` preconditions, `SwapRouterBaseIn`, reward and fee-collection rules, the limit-order effects and the state-change matrix.
+- [Fees and rewards](/products/clmm/fees): replaces the fee tiers and dynamic-fee ranges with live values, and corrects the fee side, reward settlement and collection.
+- [Code demos](/products/clmm/code-demos): fixes the increase-liquidity example, the pool-creation and limit-order notes, and the close-position warning.
+
+The [CLMM landing page](/products/clmm) checked out and is unchanged.
+
+**How to read this page.** Each change links to the affected section and supporting source. **Was** records the previous wording. **Now** records the replacement. Quotation marks indicate exact wording; "…" marks omitted text.
+
+**How it was checked.**
+
+- **Verified** against `raydium-clmm` at [`6d7a0f82`](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-clmm/tree/6d7a0f82d2f293c553c69aaf943377367c6c4cc6), the head of `master` on 2026-11-22 and the commit the docs already cite, on Anchor `1.0.2`. The TypeScript SDK source at [`32a184e`](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-sdk-V2/tree/32a184eb0aea15ddbb485e24a1a73d3723fd94d6) and the published `0.2.85-alpha` package were inspected. `scripts/check-sdk-source-identity.py` found the commit's 129 `src/` files byte-identical to the package's; the hashes are in `public/tino-changes/evidence/sdk-source-identity-2026-11-22/`. The demo repo at [`679e0c6`](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-sdk-V2-demo/tree/679e0c6cfae44ce5cc9e5eefc36c39025b7c7783) was used for comparison only.
