+- **[Math, Accumulator update](/products/clmm/math#accumulator-update):** the boundaries were off by one, and the reference reset was missing.
+  - **Was:** "0 if Δt > decay_period" … "vol_acc_prev · reduction_factor / 10,000 if filter_period < Δt ≤ decay_period" … "vol_ref_prev if Δt ≤ filter_period" … "Two rules are applied each swap"
+  - **Now:** "if Δt < filter_period" … "if filter_period ≤ Δt < decay_period" … "if Δt ≥ decay_period" … "In the last two cases the program also resets t_ref … and sets `last_update_timestamp` to now" … "The reference is updated once per swap, before the first step". The surcharge is also noted as rounded up.
+- **[Fees, Choosing parameters](/products/clmm/fees#choosing-parameters):** the "pilot pool" ranges did not describe any live config.
+  - **Was:** "Default ranges that have worked in pilot pools: | `filter_period` | 30 – 60 s |" … "| `dynamic_fee_control` | 1_000 – 50_000 |"
+  - **Now:** the four live on-chain configs (filter periods 10–30 s, `dynamic_fee_control` 1,736–99,999) and "213 of the 2,000 highest-TVL CLMM pools used a dynamic fee". The page uses the on-chain values because the API lists different ones; see [Follow-ups](#follow-ups-outside-the-clmm-chapter).
+- **[Instructions, `CreateDynamicFeeConfig`](/products/clmm/instructions#createdynamicfeeconfig-admin):** the valid ranges are open at the top.
+  - **Was:** "`reduction_factor: u16 // 1..10_000`" … "`dynamic_fee_control: u32 // 1..100_000`"
+  - **Now:** "1..9_999 (of 10_000)" … "1..99_999 (of 100_000)", and that `max_volatility_accumulator × tick_spacing` must fit in a `u32`.
