+## Tick arrays and positions
+
+Only opening a position or a limit order creates a tick array; every pool gets its bitmap extension at creation. Source: [open_position.rs](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-clmm/blob/6d7a0f82d2f293c553c69aaf943377367c6c4cc6/programs/amm/src/instructions/open_position.rs) · [increase_liquidity_v2.rs L31–36](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-clmm/blob/6d7a0f82d2f293c553c69aaf943377367c6c4cc6/programs/amm/src/instructions/increase_liquidity_v2.rs#L31-L36) · [create_pool.rs L84–93](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-clmm/blob/6d7a0f82d2f293c553c69aaf943377367c6c4cc6/programs/amm/src/instructions/create_pool.rs#L84-L93)
+
+- **[Accounts](/products/clmm/accounts#tickarraystate), [Ticks and positions, When an array is created](/products/clmm/ticks-and-positions#when-an-array-is-created) and [Instructions](/products/clmm/instructions#instruction-inventory):**
+  - **Was:** "the first position or swap that touches an uninitialized array creates it" … "`OpenPosition*` and `IncreaseLiquidity*` call `TickArrayState::get_or_create_tick_array`" … "| `SwapV2` | Possibly new `tickArrayState` |"
+  - **Now:** "`OpenPosition*` and `OpenLimitOrder` call `TickArrayState::get_or_create_tick_array`" … "`IncreaseLiquidity*` cannot create one" … "| `SwapV2` | — |"
+- **[Accounts, Account inventory and `TickArrayBitmapExtension`](/products/clmm/accounts#tickarraybitmapextension):**
+  - **Was:** "| `TickArrayBitmapExtension` | … | 0 or 1 |" … "Full-range positions (e.g., `(MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK)`) require it"
+  - **Now:** "Created by every pool-creation instruction. | 1 |" … "512 arrays of 60 ticks reach `MAX_TICK = 443636` at a spacing of 15 or more, so smaller spacings need the extension."
+- **[Overview, What CLMM is not](/products/clmm/overview#what-clmm-is-not) and [Ticks and positions, Tick spacing](/products/clmm/ticks-and-positions#tick-spacing):** width does not change the cost.
+  - **Was:** "Each new tick-array the position crosses must be initialized, costing rent. Wide ranges are cheaper; narrow ones are not." … "the cheaper to open a wide position"
+  - **Now:** "That is at most two tick arrays, whatever the range's width." … "A position never pays for more than the two arrays holding its endpoints, whatever its width."
+- **[Ticks and positions, Positions as NFTs](/products/clmm/ticks-and-positions#positions-as-nfts) and [Accounts, Position NFT mint](/products/clmm/accounts#position-nft-mint):** authority and metadata. Source: [open_position.rs L785–806](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-clmm/blob/6d7a0f82d2f293c553c69aaf943377367c6c4cc6/programs/amm/src/instructions/open_position.rs#L785-L806) · [decrease_liquidity_v2.rs L13–18](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-clmm/blob/6d7a0f82d2f293c553c69aaf943377367c6c4cc6/programs/amm/src/instructions/decrease_liquidity_v2.rs#L13-L18)
+  - **Was:** "the mint's authority is the CLMM program. The program keys position ownership to **whoever holds a balance in an ATA of that mint**" … "The SDK sets a reasonable `name`/`symbol` on the mint metadata."
+  - **Now:** "mints its single token to the owner, and then removes the mint authority. The pool PDA stays as freeze authority" … "**whoever signs as the authority of a token account holding that NFT**, ATA or not" … "the program itself writes the metadata: name `Raydium Concentrated Liquidity`, symbol `RCL`"
+- **[Ticks and positions, "In-range" vs "out-of-range"](/products/clmm/ticks-and-positions#%E2%80%9Din-range%E2%80%9D-vs-%E2%80%9Cout-of-range%E2%80%9D):** Source: [pool.rs L346–412](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-clmm/blob/6d7a0f82d2f293c553c69aaf943377367c6c4cc6/programs/amm/src/states/pool.rs#L346-L412)
+  - **Was:** "**Does** continue to accrue rewards if the pool's reward streams emit to out-of-range liquidity — but Raydium's default behavior is 'emit only to in-range'"
+  - **Now:** "Does **not** earn rewards either. … there is no setting that pays out-of-range positions."
