+## LP supply and pool creation
+
+The docs said a pool's LP mint supply is always exactly 100 units below `PoolState.lp_supply`. That holds only until someone burns LP tokens through the token program, which CPMM never sees; in 226 of the 615 sampled pools the gap was larger. Pool creation's LP formula, error list and account rules were also wrong, and one creation instruction had no section.
+
+- **[Accounts, `PoolState`](/products/cpmm/accounts#poolstate):** the gap between `lp_supply` and the mint's supply. Source: [pool.rs L105–106](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-cp-swap/blob/3d69122790e97cd6aff24e8ba95940793773f58c/programs/cp-swap/src/states/pool.rs#L105-L106) · `pool-lp-supply.csv`
+  - **Was:** `pub lp_supply: u64,                   // mirrors lp_mint supply` and "it is exactly 100 base units higher, because the 100 locked units are counted here but never minted."
+  - **Now:** `// the program's LP total; >= lp_mint supply + 100` and "At creation it is exactly 100 base units higher" … "The gap grows whenever a holder burns LP tokens directly through the token program" … "found a gap of exactly 100 in 389 pools and a larger gap in 226." The section also gives `PoolState::LEN == 637 bytes`.
