+## The price oracle
+
+The docs described an observation buffer that appends a new entry per slot from raw vault balances. The program spaces entries at least 15 seconds apart, adds to the newest entry in place between them, and records the fee-excluded price from before each swap. A TWAP built on the old description would pick the wrong timestamps.
+
+- **[Math, Observation update rule](/products/cpmm/math#observation-update-rule):** the rule as the program runs it. Source: [oracle.rs L11](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-cp-swap/blob/3d69122790e97cd6aff24e8ba95940793773f58c/programs/cp-swap/src/states/oracle.rs#L11) · [L78–141](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-cp-swap/blob/3d69122790e97cd6aff24e8ba95940793773f58c/programs/cp-swap/src/states/oracle.rs#L78-L141) · [pool.rs L248–254](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-cp-swap/blob/3d69122790e97cd6aff24e8ba95940793773f58c/programs/cp-swap/src/states/pool.rs#L248-L254) · [swap_base_input.rs L203–208](https://github.com/raydium-io/raydium-cp-swap/blob/3d69122790e97cd6aff24e8ba95940793773f58c/programs/cp-swap/src/instructions/swap_base_input.rs#L203-L208)
+  - **Was:** `if since_last >= MIN_OBSERVATION_INTERVAL {` … `let price0 = (vault1 << 32) / vault0;            // Q32.32-ish` … "Back-to-back swaps in the same slot may share one observation."
+  - **Now:** `if since_obs < 15:                        // OBSERVATION_UPDATE_DURATION_DEFAULT` … `price0 = y * 2^32 / x                     // token0 priced in token1, Q32.32` … "**Entries are at least 15 seconds apart.**" … "**Time before the first swap is not recorded.**" … "subtracting modulo 2^128"
+- **[Accounts, Observation](/products/cpmm/accounts#observation):** the same rule, with consumer guidance that follows from it.
+  - **Was:** "On every swap the program appends a new observation if enough time has passed since the last one." … "**Pick observations at least one block apart.**"
+  - **Now:** "It starts a new entry only when at least 15 seconds have passed since the newest entry; otherwise it adds to the newest entry in place." … "**Use windows much longer than 15 seconds.**" … "**Subtract with wrapping arithmetic.**" … "a full buffer spans at least 99 × 15 = 1,485 seconds (about 25 minutes)"
+- **Same section:** a field comment.
+  - **Was:** `pub last_update_timestamp: u64,                            // timestamp of the most recent append`
+  - **Now:** `pub last_update_timestamp: u64,                            // time of the last accumulation, new entry or in place`
+- **[Accounts, Observation](/products/cpmm/accounts#observation) and [Math, Observation update rule](/products/cpmm/math#observation-update-rule):** both pointed to CLMM for "more math", but CLMM's oracle stores a cumulative tick.
+  - **Was:** "More math in [`products/clmm/accounts`](/products/clmm/accounts)."
+  - **Now:** "CLMM's observation account has a different layout: it stores a cumulative tick, not a cumulative price."
