+### Stable AMM and routing compute
+
+The Stable AMM figure on two pages and every compute figure on the routing fees page were estimates. The 22 November sample replaces them. It read the 400 most recent successful transactions of each program through Triton. The routing sample covers ten minutes on 22 November (09:54–10:04 UTC). The Stable sample covers 3 to 5 November, because the program has had no successful transaction since 5 November 16:35 UTC; see [Follow-ups](#follow-ups-outside-the-cpmm-chapter). Stable AMM instruction tags 9 and 11 were identified from the program's own `swap_base_in` and `swap_base_out` log lines. Source: `public/tino-changes/evidence/stable-routing-2026-11-22/summary.json` and `compute-units.csv`
+
+- **[Routing fees, Compute cost](/products/routing/fees#compute-cost):** the estimates were too low for the router and for Stable AMM. They still described AMM v4 with OpenBook. The router's own cost grows by about 20,000 CU per hop; it is not fixed.
+  - **Was:** "**Fixed overhead:** ~5k CU for the router's dispatch logic and account validation." … "CPMM: ~20k–30k CU" … "AMM v4: ~40k–60k CU (includes OpenBook validation)" … "CLMM: ~50k–100k CU (tick-math heavy)" … "Stable: ~30k–40k CU" … "A route with 10 CPMM hops would cost ~305k CU, leaving room for other operations."
+  - **Now:** a table of the router call's median by route length (71,698 CU for 1 hop, 133,687 for 2, 181,963 for 3); "**Router overhead:** about 20,000 CU per hop, not a fixed amount." … "22,713 CU on 1-hop routes, 42,467 on 2-hop routes and 58,944 on 3-hop routes"; and a per-hop table: CLMM `swap_v2` 47,017 (430 hops), CPMM `swap_base_input` 28,798 (33), AMM v4 `SwapBaseIn` (v1) 16,279 (15), Stable AMM `SwapBaseIn` 94,487 (398). The 10-hop extrapolation is gone; the page says to simulate the whole route.
+- **[Stable AMM overview](/products/stable/overview), comparison table:**
+  - **Was:** "~5k–15k CU (binary search + interpolation); not measured" … "The Stable AMM figure is an estimate that has not been measured."
+  - **Now:** "≈94,500 CU (`SwapBaseIn`)" … "The Stable AMM figure comes from its last 398 successful swaps, on 2026-11-03 to 2026-11-05; the 9-account and 18-account layouts cost about the same." The medians were 94,084 CU for 231 swaps in the 9-account layout and 94,863 CU for 167 in the 18-account one.
